INT. ORBITAL GREENHOUSE - HELIX STATION - "DAY" CYCLE

A great curved garden turning slowly in space. Glass arches filled with starlight. Rows of tomato vines, lemon dwarfs, stalks of corn, all tied to trellises with soft cord. A gentle hum of pumps. Water droplets drift, glittering.

DR. HELENA VASQUEZ-OLUWO, 50s, botanist, floats upside down among the tomatoes with a clipboard strapped to her wrist. She is pinching a leaf, frowning.

Below her, hands on a rail, ENGINEER JOSEPHINE "JO" ARDEN, 30s, in a gray station jumpsuit, adjusts a valve and watches the readout.

HELENA
It's yellowing.

JO
The whole row?

HELENA
Half.

JO
Is it the light?

HELENA
It isn't the light.

JO
Then the water.

HELENA
It isn't the water either.

JO
Then what?

Helena pulls herself down the trellis. She hangs beside Jo. She holds out the leaf. It crumbles to powder in her fingers.

JO (CONT'D)
That's not blight.

HELENA
No.

JO
That's... static.

HELENA
Yes. She thinks so too.

JO
Who?

HELENA
Commander Rhee. She came by this morning.

JO
She didn't tell me.

HELENA
She doesn't tell you things.

JO
She tells you.

HELENA
She asks me things. It isn't the same.

Jo's jaw works. She taps the readout. Numbers scroll in amber. She stops on one.

JO
Helena. That's radiation.

HELENA
I know.

JO
From where?

HELENA
From outside.

JO
That's impossible. The shielding's rated for...

HELENA
It was rated for the old sun.

Jo turns slowly. They look at each other. A droplet of water drifts between them and breaks against the glass.

The station intercom chimes. A calm voice.

COMMANDER RHEE (V.O.)
All hands. Report to the central deck. All hands.

JO
That's her.

HELENA
Of course it is.

Jo pushes off the rail. Helena grabs a handful of leaves, stuffs them in her pocket. They float down the long arc of the garden toward the airlock, side by side. Behind them, the tomatoes turn from red to gray.

At the bulkhead, a TEENAGE CADET, 17, in an oversized uniform, drifts into their path, wide-eyed, a tablet clutched to her chest.

CADET LISANDRA
Doctor. Engineer. The Commander says it's the sun.

JO
We know.

CADET LISANDRA
She says there's a window. Eleven hours.

HELENA
For what?

CADET LISANDRA
To decide.

Helena closes her eyes. Jo takes the tablet from the cadet's hands and reads it. Then, very slowly, she hands it back. She turns her gaze to Helena. Helena doesn't open her eyes.

HELENA
Tell me.

JO
We can evacuate half.

HELENA
Which half?

JO
Whichever half she says.

HELENA
And the rest?

JO
She says they'll have the garden.

HELENA
(a bitter breath)
The garden's dying.

JO
She knows.

Cadet Lisandra stares from one woman to the other. She says nothing. A single drop of water drifts up and pops on her sleeve.

Then, beyond the arches, a flare lights the stars.

Jo and Helena turn together toward the glass. The light climbs, white and silent, across their faces.

CADET LISANDRA (CONT'D)
(whispering)
That wasn't the sun.

JO
No.

HELENA
(low)
That was the shield failing.

The hum of the pumps rises. The vines shiver on their trellises. The sirens begin.

TECHNICIAN WU, 20s, bursts through the bulkhead, goggles up, breathless.

TECHNICIAN WU
Helena! Jo! The Commander wants you on the deck now!

HELENA
We're coming, Wu.
